  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "<p>Established in 1970, North Seattle College is a public community college in the Northgate neighbourhood of Seattle, Washington. The College is a starting point for students who want to transfer to the highest-performing universities. It attracts around 14,000 students per year. The College offers many academic and career-oriented programs, including transfer degrees, professional and technical certificates, and workforce training. The small class sizes, staff support and focus on student success inspire students to achieve their educational goals.</p><h2>What is the North Seattle College acceptance rate for International Students?</h2><p>The North Seattle College acceptance rate is 100%.</p> <p>Student success is a crucial focus for the College, reflected in its facilities.  There are multiple study areas too. The library houses a wealth of information and resources. </p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>North Seattle College is situated in the Northgate area. The campus includes environmentally sensitive wetlands, which have inspired a college-wide commitment to sustainability. An artistic atmosphere pervades the campus, with opportunities for creative expression, natural landscapes, and yoga classes all inspiring students to invest in their overall well-being.</p>"
